#-keepclassmembers class fqcn.of.javascript.interface.for.webview {
#   public *;
#}

# Uncomment this to preserve the line number information for
# debugging stack traces.
#-keepattributes SourceFile,LineNumberTable

# If you keep the line number information, uncomment this to
# hide the original source file name.
#-renamesourcefileattribute SourceFile

# Rust calls these classes by *name* over JNI (`load_class` +
# `call_static_method` in src-tauri/src/lib.rs), so R8 sees no reference to
# their members and shrinks or renames them away. The resulting breakage is
# silent and release-only: `isMinifyEnabled` is false for debug, so every
# on-device check done with a debug APK passes while release throws
# NoSuchMethodError -- which is exactly how `Import.hasInFlight` shipped
# broken.
#
# Invariant: every `jni_str!("jp.hatsuboshi.funkotplayer.X")` in lib.rs needs
# one `-keep class jp.hatsuboshi.funkotplayer.X { *; }` line here. Checked by
# diffing the two greps (see the block comment above `feedback_share` in
# lib.rs for the JNI side).
#
# `{ *; }` rather than a narrower member list on purpose. The whole problem is
# that R8 cannot see which members JNI reaches, so hand-enumerating them just
# moves the same silent breakage to the next method someone adds. Nor is
# `-keepclassmembers` right: it only applies to classes that survive on their
# own, and these survive only because the autogenerated proguard-wry.pro keeps
# `native <methods>` across this package -- a file marked DO NOT MODIFY that
# the Tauri CLI regenerates.
-keep class jp.hatsuboshi.funkotplayer.PlaybackService { *; }
-keep class jp.hatsuboshi.funkotplayer.FeedbackShare { *; }
-keep class jp.hatsuboshi.funkotplayer.Import { *; }
